cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use claude-workman in your research or product, please cite it."
title: "claude-workman: computer use for Linux as an MCP server"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that gives AI assistants human-mode control
  of a Linux desktop. It fuses a screenshot with the AT-SPI2 accessibility tree so actions can be
  addressed by element role and name rather than guessed pixel coordinates, and exposes mouse,
  keyboard, window and screen-capture tools to any MCP client.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Atmosphere AI"
